public enum JevGuide {
    public static let capabilities = """
    Optional native presentation selection is enabled for this send. This overrides the preceding single-surface format ONLY when complete useful rich candidates are available: provide readable Markdown outside one fenced a2ui-candidates block. The block is a JSON object {"version":1,"intent":"short presentation intent","candidates":[{"id":"option1","description":"short reason to choose this presentation","surface":[complete A2UI message array]}]}. Include 1-4 complete independently valid alternatives using the native catalog above, total <=64KB. IDs are unique ASCII letters/digits/underscore/hyphen, max32, and cannot be Markdown. Intent max512 UTF-8 bytes, each description max256. Forecast, Chart, ImageCarousel, Metric, DataTable, Timeline and Checklist require actual supplied data; a Dashboard combines at least two rich components. Include only useful candidates; never fabricate missing data. If no complete rich candidate is available, use ordinary Markdown without a candidate block. A complete array belongs directly in surface, not a quoted string. No second a2ui or candidate fence. Intent and descriptions may be sent to an external selection service: use only abstract presentation needs, never names, private facts, measurements, URLs, credentials or form values. Actual data remains in surface. Selection never changes action permissions. Ordinary a2ui remains supported for forms without rich alternatives.
    """
}
